{"id": "xbrunei", "name": "Ulu Temburong National Park", "short": "Ulu Temburong", "place": "Brunei", "lat": 4.55, "lon": 115.15, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Brunei", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Fig and dipterocarp rainforest, hornbills, gibbons and clouded leopards.", "tip": {"id": "fig", "title": "Remove the fig trees", "text": "Figs feed birds and mammals through the forest. Set Fig trees to -100% and watch hornbills, gibbons and macaques, then the predators that hunt them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Ulu Temburong National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulu_Temburong_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Temburong District", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temburong_District"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Sunda clouded leopard", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunda_clouded_leopard"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Rhinoceros hornbill", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoceros_hornbill"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Reticulated python", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reticulated_python"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Eastern grey gibbon", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_grey_gibbon"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Ulu Temburong National Park", "icon": "aspen", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "dipt", "sp": "dipterocarpus", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Dipterocarps such as Dipterocarpus, Shorea and Dryobalanops dominate the lowland forest here and form its tall canopy."}, {"id": "fig", "sp": "ficus", "xh": 0.36, "desc": "Fruiting figs and geocarpic figs grow widely in the park, and birds feed on them."}, {"id": "aglaia", "sp": "aglaia elliptica", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "pinanga", "sp": "pinanga", "xh": 0.84}, {"id": "pig", "sp": "sus barbatus", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "macaque", "sp": "macaca fascicularis", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "An adaptable monkey that eats fruit, seeds and small animals and is recorded in the park area."}, {"id": "gibbon", "sp": "hylobates funereus", "xh": 0.34}, {"id": "prevost", "sp": "callosciurus prevostii", "xh": 0.48}, {"id": "rhino", "sp": "buceros rhinoceros", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "A large forest bird, well recorded here. Mostly fruit, but it also takes insects, small reptiles and other small animals."}, {"id": "bee", "sp": "apis dorsata", "xh": 0.76}, {"id": "stick", "sp": "haaniella echinata", "xh": 0.9}, {"id": "civet", "sp": "paradoxurus hermaphroditus", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "A night-active omnivore that eats fruit and small animals. GloBI records it eating Aglaia fruit near the park.", "ic": "fox"}, {"id": "lizard", "sp": "bronchocela cristatella", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "bronze", "sp": "dendrelaphis caudolineatus", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "frog", "sp": "polypedates leucomystax", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "beeeater", "sp": "merops viridis", "xh": 0.9}, {"id": "leopard", "sp": "neofelis diardi", "xh": 0.3, "tl": 4, "desc": "The largest carnivore on Borneo. Reported prey include deer, bearded pigs and primates."}, {"id": "python", "sp": "malayopython reticulatus", "xh": 0.65, "tl": 4, "desc": "An ambush hunter that squeezes its prey. Small ones eat rodents, bigger ones take civets and primates."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.05, "desc": "Equatorial sun feeds both the tall canopy and the plants that survive in the shade below."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "year-round rain", "xh": 0.3, "wiki": "Rain forest", "desc": "Heavy rain keeps the lowland rainforest wet, with rivers such as the Temburong and Belalong running through it."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil & nutrients", "xh": 0.55, "desc": "Leaf litter and dead wood return nutrients to the soil, where tree roots take them up again."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.8, "name": "Termites, fungi & bacteria", "desc": "Break down fallen leaves